Q: SSO using Entra ID in ASP.NET Core app as additional login option A: <p>Answering incase this is still useful. The middleware generates <code>state</code> itself, protects it, and stores a correlation cookie alongside. Don't build the link, and only challenge OIDC when the user clicks, like below:</p>
<pre><code>[HttpPost]
public IActionResult SsoLogin(string returnUrl = &quot;/&quot;)
{
    var props = new AuthenticationProperties { RedirectUri = returnUrl };
    return Challenge(props, OpenIdConnectDefaults.AuthenticationScheme);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Also drop <code>MyDataProtector</code>. Same for the <code>StringDataFormat</code> override. Delete both lines and let the defaults run.</p>
<p>Ans since you're on ASP.NET Core Identity, set the sign-in scheme so the result lands in the external cookie:</p>
<pre><code>options.SignInScheme = IdentityConstants.ExternalScheme;
</code></pre>
<p>Then your callback can use the normal external login flow, <code>GetExternalLoginInfoAsync()</code>, pull the email claim, and match it to a local user.</p>
